From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:29:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the SPI1 controller

The SoC dtsi describes no SPI controller. Boards that bring SPI1 out on
a pin header cannot use it.

Add SPI1 at 0x02541000. The manual describes it as the instance with the
display bus interface (DBI) next to the plain SPI mode, which is the
binding's "allwinner,sun60i-a733-spi-dbi" compatible. In SPI mode it has
64-entry TX and RX FIFOs and dual and quad master modes, which is what
spi-sun6i assumes for the "allwinner,sun55i-a523-spi" fallback, so the
driver binds through the binding's fallback chain and uses the plain SPI
mode. The node has the bus clock, the module clock SPI1_CLK, the reset
and DMA request 24 of DMAC0 for both directions (manual, 13.1).

Add the pin groups that reach the Cubie A7S header J11, all function 6:
clock, MOSI and MISO on PD11 to PD13, and chip select 0 on PD10 in a
group of its own, so that a board can use a GPIO chip select. The node
is disabled; a board enables it.

Not covered: chip select 1, HOLD and WP, where PD14 (HOLD) is a plain
GPIO pin on the header; the DBI mode, which the driver does not have.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with the node enabled in a copy of the DTB and
MOSI bridged to MISO on the header, 256-byte full-duplex transfers, which
go through DMA, read back unchanged at 1 MHz and 10 MHz.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 30 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 599e9a00e2d8..d0677503b443 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -595,6 +595,20 @@ spdif_out_pb_pin: spdif-pb-pin {
 				function = "spdif";
 			};
 
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			spi1_cs0_pd_pin: spi1-cs0-pd-pin {
+				pins = "PD10";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <6>;
+				function = "spi1";
+			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			spi1_pd_pins: spi1-pd-pins {
+				pins = "PD11", "PD12", "PD13";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <6>;
+				function = "spi1";
+			};
+
 			uart0_pb_pins: uart0-pb-pins {
 				pins = "PB9", "PB10";
 				allwinner,pinmux = <2>;
@@ -871,6 +885,22 @@ spdif: spdif@2537000 {
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		spi1: spi@2541000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-spi-dbi",
+				     "allwinner,sun55i-a523-spi-dbi",
+				     "allwinner,sun55i-a523-spi";
+			reg = <0x02541000 0x1000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 25 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_SPI1>, <&ccu CLK_SPI1>;
+			clock-names = "ahb", "mod";
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_SPI1>;
+			dmas = <&dma 24>, <&dma 24>;
+			dma-names = "rx", "tx";
+			status = "disabled";
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+		};
+
 		sid: efuse@3006000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-sid",
 				     "allwinner,sun50i-a64-sid";
